cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite both this software and the associated paper (see preferred-citation)."
type: software
title: "Spatial-Organellomics: manuscript analysis code"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility hub and manuscript-level analysis code for the spatial
  Organellomics (sOrganellomics) study of multi-organelle architecture in mouse
  liver and pancreas. Contains Python analysis scripts organized by figure,
  covering cross-organ principal component analysis, Gaussian mixture model
  clustering of hepatocyte organelle signatures, selection of optimal cluster
  number and principal components, harmonized benchmarking of Gaussian mixture
  and Leiden clustering against spatial molecular datasets, organelle feature
  heatmaps and subtype proportions, ANOVA / Levene / Welch / Games-Howell
  pairwise testing, spatial distribution and niche metrics, cross-modal
  proteomic alignment and proteome inference, heterogeneity indices for
  nutritional perturbation, probabilistic trajectory inference from control to
  fasted states, intravital TMRM grouping and structure-function coupling,
  multilayer perceptron prediction of nutritional state and early MASLD
  progression, and logistic regression, random forest and SHAP feature-importance
  analyses. This repository also links the reusable liv_zones segmentation and
  feature-extraction workflow, the processed source data deposited on Figshare,
  and the reused public spatial proteomic and transcriptomic datasets.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-03"
license: MIT
